<blockquote>
<p>All fabricated records of SCP-XXXX are to acknowledge it's existence and advise against interaction with the creature.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;it's&quot; should be &quot;its&quot;.</p>
<p>I feel like the second footnote is unnecessary, I think the reader can fill in easily enough what it means for something to go missing.</p>
<p>You have a few instances where you seem to have trouble deciding if SCP-XXXX is plural or singular, using &quot;are&quot; in some cases and &quot;is&quot; in others.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX has a ~75% chance of displaying distinctive &quot;blue-ringed patterns&quot; when approached by human subjects.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel like the quotations around &quot;blue-ringed patterns&quot; are unnecessary.</p>
<p>You also have an issue with the use of the word &quot;sentient&quot;. Sentient simply means capable of thought. <em>Sapient</em> means of human-level intelligence. After they find out if can communicate via written language, they would refer to it as sapient.</p>
<p>That's really all I have! SPaG is great other than the few things I mentioned above, and overall I love the content. It kept me interested and the test at the end was brilliant. This would get a +1 from me for sure!</p>
</div>
